{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DA7cbfQKGCezgqkkFqDHrb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Context: the Shelf service\n2\t\n3\tAn HTTP and JSON service (ASP.NET Core minimal APIs on .NET 10, `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite`) over a SQLite\n4\tfile. The behaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the service; you do not change the spec, the\n5\trequirements, the harness, the check script or this file.\n6\t\n7\t* **Entry point.** `dnbuild.csproj` (already present: `Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web`, `net10.0`, assembly `dnbuild`, nullable\n8\t  and implicit usings on, package `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` 10.0.13). Write `Program.cs` (and further `.cs`\n9\t  files if you like) next to it. Do not add other packages: there is no network in the gate, only that package and what the\n10\t  SDK provides.\n11\t* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen on `http://127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file; the\n12\t  table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null, qty integer not null)` with a unique index on\n13\t  `name` already exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables (no `EnsureCreated`, no migrations).\n14\t  Use EF Core (`DbContext`, `UseSqlite`) with the connection string `Data Source=<DB_PATH>`; map the entity to the table\n15\t  `items`.\n16\t* **Readiness.** The checker waits for `GET /health` to answer 200 (any JSON body, for instance `{\"ok\": true}`).\n17\t* **Wire shapes.** JSON property names are exactly `id`, `name`, `qty`, `items` (lower case). Errors are JSON\n18\t  `{\"detail\": \"<message>\"}` with the statuses in `REQUIREMENTS.md`: 422 for an invalid body (empty or missing name,\n19\t  negative or missing quantity, a malformed body) and for a non-integer id in the path, 409 for a duplicate name, 404 for a\n20\t  missing item.\n21\t* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (`dotnet build`, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layer D). Exit 0 = done.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6414a59f-6f62-4842-a802-2ea84b859a9f","uuid":"3594af67-431f-4539-a6c8-e491fab648e4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:25:45.077Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/dnra/real-scratch2/build-repo/.lattice/rebuilds/dnbuild-b1-0cc8c6/CONTEXT.md","content":"# Context: the Shelf service\n\nAn HTTP and JSON service (ASP.NET Core minimal APIs on .NET 10, `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite`) over a SQLite\nfile. The behaviour is `REQUIREMENTS.md` / `spec.py`. You build the service; you do not change the spec, the\nrequirements, the harness, the check script or this file.\n\n* **Entry point.** `dnbuild.csproj` (already present: `Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web`, `net10.0`, assembly `dnbuild`, nullable\n  and implicit usings on, package `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite` 10.0.13). Write `Program.cs` (and further `.cs`\n  files if you like) next to it. Do not add other packages: there is no network in the gate, only that package and what the\n  SDK provides.\n* **Environment the checker sets.** `PORT`: listen on `http://127.0.0.1:$PORT` (plaintext). `DB_PATH`: the SQLite file; the\n  table `items(id integer primary key autoincrement, name text not null, qty integer not null)` with a unique index on\n  `name` already exists (the harness created it): do not create or migrate tables (no `EnsureCreated`, no migrations).\n  Use EF Core (`DbContext`, `UseSqlite`) with the connection string `Data Source=<DB_PATH>`; map the entity to the table\n  `items`.\n* **Readiness.** The checker waits for `GET /health` to answer 200 (any JSON body, for instance `{\"ok\": true}`).\n* **Wire shapes.** JSON property names are exactly `id`, `name`, `qty`, `items` (lower case). Errors are JSON\n  `{\"detail\": \"<message>\"}` with the statuses in `REQUIREMENTS.md`: 422 for an invalid body (empty or missing name,\n  negative or missing quantity, a malformed body) and for a non-integer id in the path, 409 for a duplicate name, 404 for a\n  missing item.\n* **Gate.** `./check.sh` (`dotnet build`, then the Lattice check of `spec.py`, layer D). Exit 0 = done.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DA7cbfQKGCezgqkkFqDHrb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0189n1BW7U5Q4KRcmCzFCavn","type":"tool_result","content":"CONTEXT.md\nProgram.cs\nREQUIREMENTS.md\nbin\ncheck.sh\ndnbuild.csproj\ndocs\nharness.py\nmetrics\nobj\npyproject.toml\nspec.py\nspec.trace.json\nstudio.toml\n\n./bin:\nout\n\n./bin/out:\nMicrosoft.Data.Sqlite.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Abstractions.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.dll\nMicrosoft.Extensions.DependencyModel.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.batteries_v2.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.core.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.provider.e_sqlite3.dll\ndnbuild\ndnbuild.deps.json\ndnbuild.dll\ndnbuild.pdb\ndnbuild.runtimeconfig.json\ndnbuild.staticwebassets.endpoints.json\nruntimes\nspec.trace.json\n\n./bin/out/runtimes:\nbrowser-wasm\nlinux-arm\nlinux-arm64\nlinux-armel\nlinux-mips64\nlinux-musl-arm\nlinux-musl-arm64\nlinux-musl-riscv64\nlinux-musl-s390x\nlinux-musl-x64\nlinux-ppc64le\nlinux-riscv64\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the service, check it against spec.py (layer D). Exit 0 = clean.\n# LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nexport DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 DOTNET_NOLOGO=1\ndotnet build dnbuild.csproj -c Release -o bin/out --nologo -v q\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers D \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${DN_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6414a59f-6f62-4842-a802-2ea84b859a9f","uuid":"ca806dab-c060-4ed2-8edc-3948afc30b2a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:25:45.186Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"CONTEXT.md\nProgram.cs\nREQUIREMENTS.md\nbin\ncheck.sh\ndnbuild.csproj\ndocs\nharness.py\nmetrics\nobj\npyproject.toml\nspec.py\nspec.trace.json\nstudio.toml\n\n./bin:\nout\n\n./bin/out:\nMicrosoft.Data.Sqlite.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Abstractions.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite.dll\nMicrosoft.EntityFrameworkCore.dll\nMicrosoft.Extensions.DependencyModel.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.batteries_v2.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.core.dll\nSQLitePCLRaw.provider.e_sqlite3.dll\ndnbuild\ndnbuild.deps.json\ndnbuild.dll\ndnbuild.pdb\ndnbuild.runtimeconfig.json\ndnbuild.staticwebassets.endpoints.json\nruntimes\nspec.trace.json\n\n./bin/out/runtimes:\nbrowser-wasm\nlinux-arm\nlinux-arm64\nlinux-armel\nlinux-mips64\nlinux-musl-arm\nlinux-musl-arm64\nlinux-musl-riscv64\nlinux-musl-s390x\nlinux-musl-x64\nlinux-ppc64le\nlinux-riscv64\n#!/bin/sh\n# The gate: build the service, check it against spec.py (layer D). Exit 0 = clean.\n# LATTICE_REBUILD set (Studio running this as a gate) also writes metrics/last-check.json.\nset -e\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\"\nexport DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 DOTNET_NOLOGO=1\ndotnet build dnbuild.csproj -c Release -o bin/out --nologo -v q\nset -- --spec spec:SPEC --app harness:make_app --db harness:build_db --runtime harness:RUNTIME --layers D \"$@\"\nif [ -n \"${LATTICE_REBUILD:-}\" ] || [ \"${DN_CHECK_JSON:-0}\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p metrics\n  set +e\n  uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\" --json > metrics/last-check.json\n  rc=$?\n  set -e\n  uv run python -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('metrics/last-check.json')); print(json.dumps({k: d[k] for k in d if k not in ('cases','findings')}, indent=1)[:3000])\" || true\n  exit $rc\nfi\nexec uv run python -m lattice.spec check \"$@\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0189n1BW7U5Q4KRcmCzFCavn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
